# `sse_i32`'s arithmetic width vs C — a census, a fix, and a REFUTED hypothesis

host: Apple M4 Pro (darwin 25.5.0), base commit `d2ef9fb65`
oracle: `svt_full_distortion_kernel32_bits_c`, `reference/svt-av1/Source/Lib/
        Codec/pic_operators.c:86-87`
records: `sse_i32_ovf_census_2026-08-11.tsv` (this run's per-cell counts)

## 0. Headline

- The hypothesis that `sse_i32`'s 32-bit subtraction explains issue #15's
  partial-superblock RD divergence is **DEAD**. 0 wraps in **59,088,480**
  elements across 127 real-content cells — including all 67 cells that diverge
  from C. Max |difference| observed: **788**, against an i32 ceiling of
  2,147,483,647 (a factor of 2.7 million).
- The width bug was real and is **fixed anyway** (it diverged from C's
  contract, and it left `residual_recon_distortion_all_tiers_match_core` RED on
  `main`). The fix is **byte-inert**: 0 of 648 unaligned real-content cells and
  0 of 168 fingerprint cells moved.
- #15 is therefore **still open and still un-root-caused**. One more suspect is
  eliminated; nothing is explained.

## 1. What was wrong

`crates/svtav1-dsp/src/residual.rs`, `sse_i32_core`:

```rust
let e = (x - y) as i64;     // subtract in i32, THEN widen
d += (e * e) as u64;
```

C promotes both operands first — `(int64_t)(coeff[i]) - (recon_coeff[i])` — so
its difference of two `int32_t` can never wrap. Three widths differ, not one:

| site | port (before) | C | consequence |
|---|---|---|---|
| subtraction | i32, wraps | `int64_t`, exact | wrong distortion outside i32 |
| square | `i64 *`, debug-panics | `SQR((int64_t))`, wraps | debug/release divergence |
| accumulator | `u64 +=`, debug-panics | `uint64_t`, wraps | **this is what was RED** |

The red test's panic was `attempt to add with overflow` at the ACCUMULATOR, not
at the subtraction — the test's synthetic coefficients (`i32 >> 0..19`) sum
past 2^64. Both were fixed; only the accumulator was making the test red.

The NEON arm had the same i32 subtraction via `vsubq_s32`. The x86-64 `v3` arm
delegates to the scalar core and inherited the fix for free.

## 2. Task 1 — the probe, and its answer

Instrument: `residual::ovf_probe` (feature `__ovf_probe`, off by default). It
re-walks every `(a, b)` pair the encoder scores and counts, per element, the
wrapping i32 difference against the exact widened one, plus the per-call
distortion under both forms.

Positive control first (`residual::ovf_probe::ovf_probe_counts_a_real_wrap`):
on `[i32::MAX, 5, i32::MIN, 7] - [-1, 3, 1, 7]` the census reads exactly 2. A
zero from this probe is a measured zero, not a probe that never ran.

The three cells the brief named, plus one large aligned control:

| cell | port vs C | calls | elements | diff_wraps | max abs coeff | max abs diff |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| terminal 96x88 p4 qp33 (the #15 reproducer) | **DIFFERS** 521 vs 523 B | 2,062 | 198,176 | **0** | 9,620 | 163 |
| gradient 96x88 p4 qp33 (same dims, matches) | IDENTICAL 827 B | 1,066 | 272,896 | 0 | 12,958 | 117 |
| terminal 64x64 p4 qp33 (aligned control) | IDENTICAL 297 B | 989 | 85,760 | 0 | 9,620 | 165 |
| clic photo 2048x2048 p8 qp40 (large aligned) | IDENTICAL 9,649 B | 1,393 | 1,193,536 | 0 | 12,209 | 190 |

Widened to the whole divergent set — all 67 DIFFERS cells of
`unaligned_real_identity_2026-08-11.tsv` plus 60 IDENTICAL ones:

```
cells=127  calls=285,837  elements=59,088,480
diff_wraps=0  term_differs=0  call_differs=0  acc_wraps=0
max_abs_coeff=18,648  max_abs_diff=788
```

**The link does not exist.** The distortion the port fed its RD search was the
same number C's was, on every cell that diverges. This also independently
confirms the range assumption in C's own 8-bit NEON kernel
(`ASM_NEON/picture_operators_intrinsic_neon.c`, the `#else` arm): coefficients
stay inside int16, so its `vmulq_s32` low-32-bit square is exact too, and all
three forms — C scalar, C NEON, port — agree bit for bit on real input.

Not measured: 10-bit. The census ran the 8-bit 4:2:0 path only.

## 3. Task 2 — the fix, and what it cost the bitstream

Scalar/`v3`: `(x as i64) - (y as i64)`, `wrapping_mul`, `wrapping_add`.

NEON: `vsubl_s32` gives the exact widened difference, but there is no
i64xi64 multiply in NEON to square it with, and synthesising a 64x64 square
from 32-bit halves costs more than the kernel. So the arm keeps `vsubq_s32` and
DETECTS the only case where that is not C's answer — an i32 subtraction wraps
iff it differs from the saturating one — by ORing `vsubq_s32 ^ vqsubq_s32` into
a witness (3 instructions per 4 lanes, no reduction inside the loop) and
returning the exact scalar core if the witness is nonzero at the end. Fast path
exact, slow path exact, no tier left silently wrapping.

Byte consequence — **none measured**, on every grid available:

| gate | result |
|---|---|
| `byteid_fingerprint.sh` (168 cells, 32..2048) | 168/168 == C before AND after; **0 cells moved** (md5 set-diff by name) |
| `unaligned_identity_scan.sh` (648 real-content cells) | 581 identical / 67 differ, before AND after; **0 cells changed** verdict or byte count |
| `partial_sb_gate.sh` | 146/146 |
| `decode_gate_grid.sh` | 120/120 aomdec+dav1d, 120/120 == C |
| `recon_parity.sh` | 432/432 (CDEF fired on 199 streams, Wiener on 118) |
| `cargo test --workspace` | 1,031 passed, 0 failed |

That is the expected result given section 2: with zero wraps, the two forms are
the same arithmetic. It is reported as a measurement, not as a prediction.

## 4. The gate, and proof it has teeth

`sse_i32_matches_c_widths_at_i32_extremes` checks every tier against an `i128`
oracle reduced mod 2^64 — an oracle that shares no code with the kernel. Six
cases put the wrap in the vector body, in the scalar tail, below one vector,
and in the accumulator; the test ASSERTS that 5 of the 6 discriminate an i32
subtraction from C's i64 one, so the case set cannot silently go vacuous. (One
case did: two symmetric `i32::MAX` terms have mod-2^64 errors of +-2^33 that
CANCEL. It was changed to `i32::MAX` / `i32::MAX - 5`.)

Three planted mutations, each caught:

| mutation | result |
|---|---|
| NEON fallback disabled (`if false && vmaxvq_u32(wrapped) != 0`) | FAIL `sse_i32 case 0`: left 8, right 18446744004990074888 |
| scalar core back to `x.wrapping_sub(y) as i64` | FAIL `scalar core, case 0`: left 8, right 18446744004990074888 |
| `sq_sum` accumulator back to `d += ...` | FAIL (overflow panic), and it takes the pre-existing tier test down with it |

Note what the PRE-EXISTING `residual_recon_distortion_all_tiers_match_core`
did on the first two: **passed**. Its reference is `sse_i32_core` itself, so it
gates tier-vs-tier agreement, never fidelity to C. Both tiers were wrong the
same way and it saw nothing. That is why the new test uses an outside oracle.

`#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` proven active, not read: a planted `unsafe { }` in
this file fails the build with `error: usage of an 'unsafe' block`.

## 5. NOT MEASURED — the wall cost of the fix, and the perf gap

**The NEON witness's cost is NOT MEASURED.** It adds 3 instructions per 4 lanes
(`vqsubq_s32`, `veorq_u32`, `vorrq_u32`) to a kernel family the 2026-07
re-profile put at 11.47 % of preset-6 self time. On a wide out-of-order core a
loop already carrying 2 loads + 1 sub + 2 `vmlal` may absorb them for free —
or may not. Nobody has run the A/B.

**The port-vs-C gap was NOT re-measured on the fixed build either.** The
standing numbers stay the 2026-08-11 ones (`perf_gap_2026-08-11.tsv`: slope
ratio p2 4.12x, p6 3.52x, p10 3.53x, p13 3.51x). They were taken pre-fix; since
the fix is byte-identical they are still comparing the same output, but they do
not include the witness's cost.

Why not: another agent held the box with a live interleaved timed campaign
(`bench_a0pad2` / `bench_a0rect` / `bench_a0both` rotating at 95-100 % CPU
throughout this session), and this host has no `measlock`. Measuring into that
corrupts both sides — the exact failure `rav1d-safe/docs/AGENT_BRIEF.md`
section 2 documents. A load-tagged ratio was judged not worth degrading a
neighbour's campaign for.

What to run when the box is quiet, un-niced, n >= 9:

```
cargo bench -p zenav1-svt-dsp --bench kernel_tiers     # the kernel A/B
tools/perf_gap_campaign.sh                             # ms = a + b*pixels
```

If the witness costs anything measurable, the cheaper shape to try first is
hoisting the wrap test out of the inner loop — the encoder's own census says
`max_abs_coeff` is 18,648, so a single per-call magnitude bound would license
skipping the check entirely.

## 6. Reproduce

```
cargo test -p zenav1-svt-dsp --lib residual
cargo test -p zenav1-svt-dsp --features __ovf_probe --lib ovf_probe -- --exact \
    residual::ovf_probe::ovf_probe_counts_a_real_wrap
cargo build --release -p zenav1-svt --features __ovf_probe --example identity_run
target/release/examples/identity_run crop:<png> 96 88 33 4 ~/tmp/p  # OVFPROBE on stdout
tools/byteid_fingerprint.sh out.tsv ; tools/unaligned_identity_scan.sh out2.tsv
```
